<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_Ollathrix.xml              RM_Webwork · OLLATHRIX_OWNER_SPECIES_1
  ============================================================================
  The Webwork's owner species, per
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_owner_and_nest_2026-09-23.md §1
  (S0 rulings 1-3, S1). ONE ThingDef, ONE PawnKindDef, both RM_Ollathrix, cast
  inline in RM_Webwork's own wildAnimals — no castes, no guild, no juvenile
  kind (S0 ruling 2: nettik/chirrik/rothrik are dead). The dormant ambusher
  and the roaming hunter are the SAME PawnKindDef in two states
  (CompCanBeDormant startsDormant=true — vanilla wakes it on damage or
  approach; there is no second kind for "ambusher").

  Register and look — ours, and deliberately NOT the canon Wyyyschokk in any
  of the five marks the design doc's table lists (body colour, abdomen mark,
  bristles, legs, eyes): bone-white/dead-silk-cream body with no marking,
  hairless glossy chitin with a matte silk-dust bloom, pale legs with a dark
  blade-edge, one pale ring of small colourless eyes (reads blind — it hunts
  by web-sense, not sight). The Utinni-layer skin patch
  (src/RimStarWars/Shokk/Patches/RSW_Shokk_OllathrixSkin.xml,
  SHOKK_RSW_MOD_1 successor) overlays the canon Wyyyschokk identity onto this
  SAME defName when mandrake.rsw.shokk is loaded — same shape as the Fever
  Wood's Sekkulaath -> dianoga (Q11a: an invented name is not IP, so the
  free biome carries its own owner species and the campaign layer overlays a
  skin, never a second def).

  Mechanisms built here (self-contained, no cross-mod dependency — the free
  mod must be whole per Q11a):
    - mandible bite + leg-blade slash (armour-penetration benchmark), venom
      on the bite (RM_Damage_OllathrixVenom, additionalHediffs ->
      RM_OllathrixVenom, same shape as RM_Damages_ContactVenom.xml).
    - untameable: wildness 1.0 + trainability None (ban 1: no tamed, traded
      or negotiated Ollathrix), same convention as RM_Kurreth/RM_DustHusk.
    - ambush burst: CompProperties_CanBeDormant/CompProperties_WakeUpDormant
      on the race ThingDef itself (RM_DustHusk precedent, RimWorld/
      CompWakeUpDormant.cs already read in full by that item) — wakes on
      damage or on a target approaching within wakeUpCheckRadius.

  Deliberately NOT built here (owned by other items, per the design doc's
  own §1a/§5 table — do not duplicate):
    - the mouth-loom ranged spit, the Shokk-bound hediff, sun-scald and the
      emergent-spawn comp: these are RSW-tier mechanisms today
      (mandrake.rsw.shokk, patched onto the donor Wyyyschokk) that
      SHOKK_SKIN_SHRINK_1 is tasked to move onto this race and re-token
      RM_ — wiring them here now would duplicate that item's own scope and
      leave this race depending backward on an RSW-tier mod, which the tier
      grammar forbids. Left off; SHOKK_SKIN_SHRINK_1 attaches them once it
      moves the defs down.
    - web-sense convergence (RM_JobGiver_SenseWebConverge / the race's own
      ThinkTreeDef), the droid-priority scorer, and the nest's own mother
      guardian wiring: all WEBWORK_MECHANICS_1 / WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1
      scope, unbuilt today per the design doc's own mechanism table.
    - the egg economy, the nest cluster, the carried-eggs mark: all
      WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1, a sibling item, not this one.

  Body: BeetleLikeWithClaw (same body RM_Kurreth/RM_Quarrok already use in
  this repo) — six InsectLeg parts plus a HeadClaw group on the head part,
  which the leg-blade tool links to (the same body's only clawed attack
  group; "leg-blade" is the tool's flavour name, not a claim that
  BeetleLikeWithClaw has a bespoke leg-mounted blade part).

  Art: 0 hits for "ollathrix" in infrastructure/artpipe/registry.jsonl (6588
  lines; sanity-probed against "graniteslug"/"webwork", both 30 hits, so the
  search itself is live). No existing render anywhere. Flat-colour
  placeholder generated this pass (art/Fauna/gen_ollathrix_placeholder.py,
  same shape as WEBWORK_FAUNA_ROSTER_1's own placeholder script) so it never
  renders magenta; real art queued
  (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/webwork_fauna.csv, RM_Ollathrix_v1 row).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Ollathrix</defName>
    <label>ollathrix</label>
    <labelPlural>ollathrix</labelPlural>
    <description>A spider the size of an elephant, weight for weight closer to a horse — mostly a mass of nimble, sharp legs under a low, wide, bone-white body. Its abdomen carries no mark of any kind, faintly translucent, the darker gut showing through the empty silk-cream chitin. It does not seem to see you; a raised ring of small, colourless eyes reads blind, and it hunts by feel alone, through the web that reaches every part of the thicket it owns. Those who enter the Webwork frequently discover a shadow, seconds before it lands on them, and know nothing more.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.4</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>420</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>60</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.25</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.15</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <!-- Ban 1 (no tamed, traded or negotiated Ollathrix): wildness 1.0
           alone makes taming chance effectively zero; trainability None
           below closes the rest, same paired convention RM_Kurreth and
           RM_DustHusk already use in this repo. -->
      <Wildness>1.0</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandibles</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>16</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>1</chanceFactor>
        <!-- Venom on the bite, per §1a: "venom on bite for large prey" —
             carried as a bespoke bite DamageDef rather than the generic
             Bite capacity, same shape RM_Damages_ContactVenom.xml already
             uses for a scratch. -->
        <extraMeleeDamages>
          <li>
            <def>RM_Damage_OllathrixVenom</def>
            <amount>1</amount>
          </li>
        </extraMeleeDamages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>leg-blade</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Cut</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>13</power>
        <armorPenetration>0.35</armorPenetration>
        <cooldownTime>1.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadClaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>1</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <!-- Ambush burst (§1a): the dormant ambusher and the roaming hunter
           are the SAME PawnKindDef in two states — every wild Ollathrix
           spawns lurking and wakes on damage or on a target closing to
           wakeUpCheckRadius, RM_DustHusk's own stock-comp precedent
           (RimWorld/CompWakeUpDormant.cs read in full by that item). No
           second kind, no concealment Thing (that half stays deferred,
           WEBWORK_MECHANICS_1 scope). -->
      <li Class="CompProperties_CanBeDormant">
        <startsDormant>true</startsDormant>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_WakeUpDormant">
        <wakeUpOnDamage>true</wakeUpOnDamage>
        <wakeUpCheckRadius>6</wakeUpCheckRadius>
        <wakeUpIfAnyTargetClose>true</wakeUpIfAnyTargetClose>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>BeetleLikeWithClaw</body>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>2.0</maxPreyBodySize>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <baseBodySize>2.6</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>2.2</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.4</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <fleshType>Insectoid</fleshType>
      <bloodDef>Filth_BloodInsect</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <useMeatFrom>Megaspider</useMeatFrom>
      <!-- manhunterOnDamageChance 1.0: hit it and it is now hunting you —
           the closest stock-field approximation of ban 2's "hostile to
           everything, including each other, no truce" without new C#
           faction wiring (deferred, WEBWORK_MECHANICS_1). -->
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>1.0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>14</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>10</gestationPeriodDays>
      <!-- Reproduction here is ordinary-animal flavour only: the "1,000
           eggs a year"/fecund-and-self-predating mechanic (S0 ruling 6, §4)
           is expressed by the nest's own RM_Webwork_EggClutch economy, a
           sibling item (WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1) — not by this race's
           litter. -->
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.99, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(1.01, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.2</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
          <soundWounded>Pawn_Insect_Ambient</soundWounded>
          <soundDeath>Pawn_Insect_Ambient</soundDeath>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Insectoid_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Ollathrix</defName>
    <label>ollathrix</label>
    <labelPlural>ollathrix</labelPlural>
    <race>RM_Ollathrix</race>
    <combatPower>160</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <!-- Solitary: §3a's own "every other one on the map is a roll" besides
         the nest's guaranteed mother — no wild grouping. -->
    <wildGroupSize>1~1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.1</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ollathrix/RM_Ollathrix</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>3.2</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ollathrix/RM_Ollathrix</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>4.2</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ollathrix/RM_Ollathrix</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>5.2</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
